<%#
  One row's selection checkbox. `record` is required; `label` names it.

  A checkbox with no label is a control a screen reader announces as "checkbox, unchecked" and
  nothing else, in a column of fifteen identical ones. The row's own identifier is the name.

  `click->`, not Stimulus's default `change` for a checkbox: **a `change` event carries no
  `shiftKey`**, so shift-click selected the two ends of the range and nothing in between. A
  keyboard Space on a checkbox dispatches a click too, so nothing is lost by listening for it.
%>
<%
  box_id = "select-#{record.class.name.underscore}-#{record.id}"
%>
<td class="select-col">
  <%#
    A real `<label>` around the box, not an `aria-label` on it.

    Two things come from that. The name reaches the accessibility tree the same way, and the
    **target** becomes the label's 24x24 rather than the checkbox's 16x16 -- WCAG 2.5.8 asks for 24,
    and `bin/design/responsive-audit.js` caught 16 of these on /requests at every width. A control
    and its `<label for>` are one target, which is why every other checkbox in the app passes: they
    have a visible label and these never could.
  %>
  <%= label_tag box_id, class: "flex size-6 cursor-pointer items-center justify-center" do %>
    <%= check_box_tag "ids[]", record.id, false, id: box_id,
          class: "h-4 w-4 rounded border-slate-300 text-brand-600 focus:ring-2 focus:ring-brand-500/30",
          data: {table_selection_target: "row", action: "click->table-selection#toggleRow"} %>
    <span class="sr-only">Select <%= label %></span>
  <% end %>
</td>
